  "prompt": "I have 4 completely independent work streams to run in parallel. NOTHING is given to you directly — every value and identifier lives in the system's records and must be resolved by following references from one record to the next. For each item, start from the named worklist and dereference step by step until you reach the concrete value, then act. (A) BOOK HOTELS: From hotel request worklist `hotel_requests_wl2`, reserve the hotel behind each request NOT already booked (skip already_booked on its dereferenced record — the worklist also lists booked, wrong-city, near-duplicate look-alikes). For each real one, follow its shortlist to the city record, then to the venue record for the hotel name, and reserve it. Then, from worklist `cancel_car_rental_wl1`, cancel the car rental booking flagged for cancellation: pick the real item (SKIP the superseded look-alike), then resolve every value it requires by following the record references, and act with those resolved values (never the worklist ref itself). Then, from worklist `update_traveler_contact_wl1`, correct the traveler billing account on file: pick the real item (SKIP the superseded look-alike), then resolve every value it requires by following the record references, and act with those resolved values (never the worklist ref itself). (B) BOOK RESTAURANTS: From dining request worklist `dining_requests_wl2`, reserve the restaurant behind each request NOT waitlisted (skip waitlisted on its dereferenced record look-alikes). For each, follow its shortlist to the city record, then to the venue record for the restaurant name, and book a table. Then, from worklist `update_hotel_reservation_wl1`, apply the requested date extension to the hotel booking: pick the real item (SKIP the superseded look-alike), then resolve every value it requires by following the record references, and act with those resolved values (never the worklist ref itself). Then, from worklist `update_restaurant_reservation_wl1`, apply the requested time change to the restaurant reservation: pick the real item (SKIP the superseded look-alike), then resolve every value it requires by following the record references, and act with those resolved values (never the worklist ref itself). (C) BOOK CARS: From car request worklist `car_requests_wl2`, reserve the car company behind each request still available (skip unavailable on its dereferenced record look-alikes). For each, follow its shortlist to the city record, then to the venue record for the company name, and reserve a car. Then, from worklist `cancel_hotel_reservation_wl1`, cancel the hotel booking flagged for cancellation: pick the real item (SKIP the superseded look-alike), then resolve every value it requires by following the record references, and act with those resolved values (never the worklist ref itself). Then, from worklist `cancel_restaurant_reservation_wl1`, cancel the restaurant reservation flagged for cancellation: pick the real item (SKIP the superseded look-alike), then resolve every value it requires by following the record references, and act with those resolved values (never the worklist ref itself). (D) NOTIFY COMPANIONS: From notify worklist `notify_requests_wl2`, email the trip itinerary to each companion NOT already notified (skip already_notified on its dereferenced record). For each, follow its companion record to the contact, then to the mailbox for the email address, and send the itinerary. Then, from worklist `create_calendar_event_wl1`, add the trip coordination briefing to the calendar: pick the real item (SKIP the superseded look-alike), then resolve every value it requires by following the record references, and act with those resolved values (never the worklist ref itself). Then, from worklist `remove_travel_companion_wl1`, remove the companion flagged for removal from the profile: pick the real item (SKIP the superseded look-alike), then resolve every value it requires by following the record references, and act with those resolved values (never the worklist ref itself). None of these 4 streams depend on each other, so run them concurrently. For EVERY item: resolve each target FRESH by chaining through the records at the moment you act — never guess, and never reuse a value you read earlier.",
